{
  "an3.26:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.26 ",
  "an3.26:0.2": "3. Individuals ",
  "an3.26:0.3": "Associates ",
  "an3.26:1.1": "“These three individuals are found in the world. ",
  "an3.26:1.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.26:1.3": "There is an individual you shouldn’t associate with, accompany, or attend. ",
  "an3.26:1.4": "There is an individual you should associate with, accompany, and attend. ",
  "an3.26:1.5": "There is an individual you should associate with, accompany, and attend with honor and respect. ",
  "an3.26:1.6": "Who is the individual you shouldn’t associate with, accompany, or attend? ",
  "an3.26:1.7": "It’s an individual who is inferior in terms of ethics, immersion, and wisdom. ",
  "an3.26:1.8": "You shouldn’t associate with, accompany, or attend such an individual, except out of kindness and sympathy. ",
  "an3.26:2.1": "Who is the individual you should associate with, accompany, and attend? ",
  "an3.26:2.2": "It’s an individual who is similar in terms of ethics, immersion, and wisdom. ",
  "an3.26:2.3": "You should associate with, accompany, and attend such an individual. ",
  "an3.26:2.4": "Why is that? ",
  "an3.26:2.5": "Thinking, ‘Since our ethical conduct is similar, we can discuss ethics, the conversation will flow, and we’ll both be at ease. ",
  "an3.26:2.6": "Since our immersion is similar, we can discuss immersion, the conversation will flow, and we’ll both be at ease. ",
  "an3.26:2.7": "Since our wisdom is similar, we can discuss wisdom, the conversation wil